a Demon by erasing the Idea from existence sounds interesting, might actually work with Arch-Spheres or greater levels of Abyss-Mysticism.<br /> But I can think of another possibility. You remember that Angels that went to god to see like he sees? they disappeared permanently but they were still remembered.<br /> <br /> I assume that these Angels Merged with God and therefore lost their individual existance without getting forgotten. Given that an earthbound merged with a far more powerfull being could &quot;vanish&quot; without being forgotten.<br /> <br /> So Maybe if the Earthbound is NOT one of the 5 Earthbound Mentioned by you, you could cut a deal with one of the 5 to arrange them the chance to absorb the &quot;lesser Earthbound to increase their power (Okay, it may lead to you being fucked by a far more powerfull earthbound than before o.o ).<br /> <br /> what do you think Crowley?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T12:27:14-07:00","id":151585,"title":"","content":"Lasombra with abyss mysticism could work, but I'd recommend your friendly neighborhood upstart Baali as a potential candidate if they are included in your game. Perhaps instead of focusing on banishing the Demon, you could find and use an Infernalist (probably a more foolhardy one) as a vessel, or to contain the Demon. Hell, strike a bargain with the Infernalist if need be. After that, let them be fodder for the local Sabbat Inquisitor or Sheriff to deal with. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cAnd those who were seen dancing were thought to be insane by those who could not hear the music.\u201d - Friedrich Nietzsche</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/812-datura","name":"Datura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T16:01:53-07:00","id":151789,"title":"","content":"-Contact a Giovanni<br /> -go in the Shadowlands<br /> -toss the damn thing in the Tempest<br /> -Run like hell and hope the Gehenna come before someone actually retrieve the damn ring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T17:55:28-07:00","id":151872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eadee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/150981-killing-an-earthbound?p=151564#post151564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Crowley: thats a lot of being fucked. I think I'll recommend messing with earthbound to the next nympho I meet.<br /> <br /> But the possibility of killing a Demon by erasing the Idea from existence sounds interesting, might actually work with Arch-Spheres or greater levels of Abyss-Mysticism.<br /> But I can think of another possibility. You remember that Angels that went to god to see like he sees? they disappeared permanently but they were still remembered.<br /> <br /> I assume that these Angels Merged with God and therefore lost their individual existance without getting forgotten. Given that an earthbound merged with a far more powerfull being could &quot;vanish&quot; without being forgotten.<br /> <br /> So Maybe if the Earthbound is NOT one of the 5 Earthbound Mentioned by you, you could cut a deal with one of the 5 to arrange them the chance to absorb the &quot;lesser Earthbound to increase their power (Okay, it may lead to you being fucked by a far more powerfull earthbound than before o.o ).<br /> <br /> what do you think Crowley?</div> </div> </div> </div>My two cents:<br /> <br /> Stay. Away. From. The. Archdukes.<br /> <br /> Seriously, assuming you manage to contact them and start a conversation before having your soul ripped from your body and raped (and that's a <i>really</i> <i>big</i> if), there's not much you can offer them they cannot take themselves or force others to give. Unless we're speaking about Belial and you have a spare Lucifer to sell, but good luck with that too.<br /> <br /> Lesser Earthbounds are no different: if they're stronger than the one you're dealing with, the'yre bad news. You <i>might </i>offer them something they want, but Earthbounds are the sort of beings that will enslave everyone that could be useful to them, just in case. You would indeed trade a problem with a bigger one: Earthbounds are just like that. Pure hate distilled by millenias of never-ending torment. And some of them have a grudge against Cain (and it progeny) as well.<br /> <br /> As a vampire, your best shot when dealing with an Earthbound is destroying its its cult and cut him from his Faith sustenance, then wait as far as you can. Alternatively, find his Reliquiary, make somebody else take it (you really don't want to touch that thing) and have it dropped in a on holy ground. Places like St. Peter Square or the Golgotha work best, but most churches will do. Again, the problem is taking it there.<br /> <br /> The last option I consider feasible when you're not a Demon is risky and not guaranteed to work, but it should be mentioned neverthless. Find another Earthbound, aim it to the one you're trying to deal with and hope they don't make a deal. After their cults clash, finish the job. If one Earthbound destroyed the other, all the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 05-28-2014, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T18:20:26-07:00","id":151891,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, this Demon, Moloch, doesn't have an active cult. &amp; yes he is only moderately fucked up, it's humanoid with goat legs &amp; an owl head &amp; wings, it has another twisted face on its chest &amp; it smells rank &amp; slimy, it has a four foot floppy uncircumcised dick. Is there a way I could build up his cult &amp; reach a symbiotic relationship with him? The ring seems indestructible beyond going into Mordor &amp; climbing Mt. Doom.<br /> <br /> On a side note: He can go into the spirit realm, I've thought about using this to my advantage to subtly bloodbond vampires using three bottles made with the Vitae transfer ritual. Is there any other mischief I can use this for that I haven't thought of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T18:26:46-07:00","id":151901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eadee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/150981-killing-an-earthbound?p=151564#post151564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Crowley: thats a lot of being fucked. I think I'll recommend messing with earthbound to the next nympho I meet.<br /> <br /> But the possibility of killing a Demon by erasing the Idea from existence sounds interesting, might actually work with Arch-Spheres or greater levels of Abyss-Mysticism.<br /> But I can think of another possibility. You remember that Angels that went to god to see like he sees? they disappeared permanently but they were still remembered.<br /> <br /> I assume that these Angels Merged with God and therefore lost their individual existance without getting forgotten. Given that an earthbound merged with a far more powerfull being could &quot;vanish&quot; without being forgotten.<br /> <br /> So Maybe if the Earthbound is NOT one of the 5 Earthbound Mentioned by you, you could cut a deal with one of the 5 to arrange them the chance to absorb the &quot;lesser Earthbound to increase their power (Okay, it may lead to you being fucked by a far more powerfull earthbound than before o.o ).<br /> <br /> what do you think Crowley?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok...imagine this...you got the Earthbound that created the concept of Vengeance...you kill it...NO ONE CAN EVER COMIT ANY ACT IN THE NAME OF VENGEANCE AND THIS ONE SUDDENLY VANISHES OF THE TIMESTREAM....sweet mother of paradoxes...<br /> <br /> Dealing with a demon is easy, earthbound...how do i explain ...<br /> <br /> This is the trademark that my demon (crowley) uses to take care of His victims..<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HahZprrYXnA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HahZprrYXnA</a><b> Incoming GORE </b><br /> <br /> Now...What does an earthbound does...hurmmm<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6QFwo57WKwg\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6QFwo57WKwg</a> Focus on the final sequence, not on the minor eldritch horrors...also a bit of NSFW<br /> <br /> Anyone here has read any lovecraft material? you dont Deal with the big 5 of doom, you dont ask azatoth to erase one vampire. you dont kill a fly with an atomic bomb. you dont go to cain saying &quot;your brother was lame&quot; or &quot;he doesnt look so though, here. hold mah beer.&quot; <br /> <br /> The good news about the big 5, they are mostly sleep...mostly. The bad news...well, when you wake up one of the big 5 you<br /> A) Cause a new Maelstrom<br /> B) Cause Armaggedon/Apocalypse/Gehenna/The Winter/The Reckoning<br /> <br /> As for the idea with mergin it with god...not bad but your plan has a few flaws...and im avoiding all kind of spoilers in here<br /> -NO ONE KNOWS WHERE GOD IS! and no, not even in canon. its not on earth a-la Preacher/Supernatural.<br /> -The damn bitch ran away from her creation (yes, god is a she)<br /> as for the angels...thats even more complicated to explain but lets put it this way. Whenever i run a world of darkness game and my players SEE angels or hear that there might be angels involved, they shit their pants and run away from the task at hand.<br /> <br /> Right now your priority is to Contain the earthbound.<br /> What do i mean by contain?. A, Keeping him away from the population. This might be tricky but an earthbounds powers are strong enough to affect targets that are not even in the same country. by keeping any supernatural/human away from it, you will make it harder for him to be reached by a cult or anything, this doesnt means the cult needs to be next to him to feed him, but it will be harder for It to get backup whenever shit hits the fan.<br /> <br /> Second: Domination Doesnt Works, Illusions are useless. and dementation? please....Dementation is the equivelant of trying to stop a nuclear bomb with a feather by tickling it. <br /> <br /> Third: Earthbounds have an Alien mind...they dont see things like rest of the WoD does. Why is this? every supernatural lived like a human at one point. this means, theres a concept of moral, ethics and such very stuck within human mentality and within supernaturals. Now....Hows the mind of something that was BORN being a god, never having moral, ethics, or any boundries, which made PEOPLE pray at it and give it an superiority complex?. They Dont Think like us, They dont See things like us.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, my 2 cents on operation &quot;Garbage Can.&quot;<br /> I Dm wraith....your chances on Wraithland (The underworld/stygia) are incredibly low...<br /> How will you keep the earthbound in check while you go downstairs?, how will you deal with its cult and its powers?. Toss the earthbound to the tempest..ok, then what? IF one member of his cult knows his name (angelic name) thats enough to bring him back from whatever hole he is in. same if you throw him to the abysm. He will put a hell of a fight and goind down to stygia/underworld with that thing is always trouble, between wraith hating vampires and the Spectres, your chances are not so good.<br /> <br /> Operation: walking Pi\u00f1ata<br /> Earthbounds Cant possess living vessels (same go for vampires).<br /> Ok. acording to the storyteller book of DtF, he cant do a pact with you so..you cant win anything (since vampires dont have any faith potential). Second, youre undead so...undeads cant be possessed...Ghouls on the other hand...<br /> <br /> Now, what if a Ghoul is possesed by a demon? the ghoul dies and the demon recides absorbing all of the ghouls memories..And no, the disciplines are replaced by Lores and Apocalyptic Forms.<br /> <br /> What happend when a Ghoul/human Is possessed by an Earthbound, the character literaly blows up. he will explote in a gory fashion and the earthbound will be around still. Earthbounds are so evil and twisted that no one can stand their presence. Not even werewolves (which are the ultimate badasses of the WoD)., they pop up like a pi\u00f1ata.<br /> <br /> So my friend... My only advice, as a storyteller and not a player (this is metagaming by the way) Is<br /> <br /> A ): find demons who are willing to take him down. Which will be hard enough<br /> B ): Find Imbueds who are willing to take him down...and they will likely try to kill you as well<br /> C ) Werewolves might break the vessel..but the apocalyptic form still packs the punch<br /> D ) Ask for help to the technocracy...but you'll end up fucked up.<br /> E ) Exorcise the living shit out of him and with enough luck (and human sacrifices) you might be able to throw it back to the abysm<br /> <br /> In case you take A B C D or E, you will still have to pull a manhunt on every single member of his cult, and make sure they are gone for good, as well to erase all knowledge of It. make all documents of his existance vanish...<br /> Now, if youre playing in Los Angeles, you might have the local demon court willing to help you...for a price.<br /> If youre playing in New York, ill give you my demon court stats and characters for your ST to use them as NPCs and they Might help... they recently dealt with an earthbound and they are still trying to reagroup ever since so....your chances are low.<br /> <br /> And tell that ST that he is a bastard for using an earthbound on a VtM game...only sadistic bastards to shit like that...i like your ST already xD<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T19:35:10-07:00","id":151989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aermas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/150981-killing-an-earthbound?p=151891#post151891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, this Demon, Moloch, doesn't have an active cult. &amp; yes he is only moderately fucked up, it's humanoid with goat legs &amp; an owl head &amp; wings, it has another twisted face on its chest &amp; it smells rank &amp; slimy, it has a four foot floppy uncircumcised dick. Is there a way I could build up his cult &amp; reach a symbiotic relationship with him? The ring seems indestructible beyond going into Mordor &amp; climbing Mt. Doom.<br /> <br /> On a side note: He can go into the spirit realm, I've thought about using this to my advantage to subtly bloodbond vampires using three bottles made with the Vitae transfer ritual. Is there any other mischief I can use this for that I haven't thought of?</div> </div> </div> </div>oh and...ok..Moloch...lets see on wikipedia how badass he would be..ok..his wikipedia entry game some ideas....<br /> <br /> ill be blunt, youre fucked.<br /> He is part of the pop culture. which means that people can re create his cult.....<br /> <br /> Second: his description...ermm....that might be a facade...since most earthbounds look something like this <a href=\"http://fc00.deviantart.net/fs70/f/2011/069/8/1/eldritch_abomination_by_theparanoidfreak-d3bd86e.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://fc00.deviantart.net/fs70/f/20...ak-d3bd86e.jpg</a> as Zefrank said once &quot;If you ask a 14 year old boy who happends to be a sexual deviant with a violence streak to draw you his favorite god, it would look like an earthbound.&quot; ..&quot; Which would resemble what would plop out of a nightmare that farted too agressively.&quot; <a href=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/scale_small/5/57845/1212600-xavier_ship001.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/...er_ship001.jpg</a><br /> <br /> Third: making him a cult....ok..in which city are you playing?<br /> <br /> Fourth: IF youre over 7th generation, you might be able to pull something with a ritual...If youre under generation 7th, Read and do as following.<br /> <br /> Take a Gun, Put it in your forehead. pull trigger, apply bullet directly to the forehead.<br /> If it doesnt works.<br /> Wait for the sun to be as high as possible. jump out of a window, sparkle for a second, catch fire. explote into ashes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T20:51:30-07:00","id":152066,"title":"","content":"Depends on the Earthbound. Some are phenomenally weak, so much so that the average vampire elder can fuck them up pretty hard. Others are so powerful you might as well be contending with a Tzimisce Methuselah or some other entity in-splat from VtM that can fuck you up hard core. Any Demon that can flesh-craft a Vampire is probably in the upper category, Overlord at the very least. Seeing as Demons are immune to most of the standard mind-rapey and body-fucking-up abilities (as they are not alive or mortal). Earthbound can't commit diablerie on a Vampire, thankfully, as you kind of need a Beast to do that. Now, on the plus side... it can't possess you longterm. Any Demon that tries to possess a vampire usually screams in Torment and is immediately hurled into the Abyss, don't pass Go, don't collect $200. However, Earthbound are masters of commanding and directing Torment to their own advantage (since they kind of had to or be utterly fucked themselves). Thus a particularly powerful one might be able to possess you for a time, but unless you are REALLY low generation (or have high Fortitude I'd wager) they would quickly drive you into Torpor from the consumptive and body-warping effects of their Torment. Bad news, even if the possession ends and you get your body back... you probably will end up with tentacles or as a bilateral hermaphrodite (or worse).<br /> <br /> Now, as to the means and ways of getting rid of the bastard... there are quite a few. As mentioned, any Lasombra Abyss Mystic with Obtenebration six or higher can probably banish the fucker with a simple ritual. Provided, you know, the Demon doesn't fuck it up somehow (which it might depending on its Lores, or Arcanum... depending on the version of Demon that is being run). Now, there are other options. Powerful Baali, usually sixth generation or lower, can make that Demon their bitch given time. Hell, any Baali with Daimoinon 5 can fuck that Demon up something fierce if they get a lucky roll. &quot;Hey Demon, meet Severity 5 Curse, have fun in the Abyss for... ever?&quot; Of course its also possible a powerful Koldun, Thaumaturge, or a few Methuselahs of other Clans (Valeren Eight or Obtenebration Nine can make that Demon cry for mercy pretty quickly). However, that still means you need to convince Rayzeel or Montano to be your friend. Unlikely even in the best prospects. Of course, any of the Antediluvians could destroy or banish an Earthbound laughably easily (so long as it isn't an Duke or Archduke).<br /> <br /> Beyond the stuff common in Vampire... a group of Garou Theurges with the right Rites could do it. As could some of the crazier things like Firstborn Fae who have achieved mastery of their respective Dominions, or some of the more <i>lucid </i>Mummies. Than there are Mages. Sweet, beautiful, nearly omnipotent (given preparation) Mages. Mages might not be able to command Demons with Spirit or Mind (unless they are very knowledgeable Masters or Arch-Masters), but Prime is a Demon's worse nightmare. Not only can Prime fuck up the Demon's attempt to use Lores, it can also unweave the enchantment on the ring. The Masters of Prime can even permanently destroy Demons, this is a ritual known among the Celestial Chorus (according to rumor). Arch-Masters of Prime are not that impressed by Demons, and Oracles would find anything less than the mightiest of the Earthbound to be jokes. An Exemplar of Prime... wouldn't even notice the Demon, and if it did direct it's (Exemplars are no longer &quot;he's or she's&quot;) ire at the Demon it would likely be consumed wholly in celestial fire. The only problem is that finding Mages is hard. Finding Master Mages is damn near impossible. Finding Arch-Mages is a quest worthy of the trials of Hercules. Finding an Oracle is utterly impossible if it doesn't <i>want </i>to be found. Finding an Exemplar is... unadvised.<br /> <br /> Outside of that, there are less defined means of disposable. Which are wholly dependent on the Storyteller's Crue... I mean, Imagination!<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:Just remembered. Earthbound Reliquaries grant a few immunities that require they be destroyed before those tricks I listed can even be used. Destroying a reliquary is difficult, largely due to it not having a soak pool as it instead reduces all damage rolls against it by the Earthbound Demon's Willpower in successes. The average-ish Willpower of Earthbound Demons is between 8-10, though a few are as low as 6 dots. Which makes that roughly equivalent to a Soak Pool of 12-20 dice. That is some hellish amount of damage resilience. Thankfully certain attacks (True Faith ones if I remember correctly) completely ignore that protection. Now, Earthbound Demon Lores are pretty crazy as they can have anywhere between six and fourty-eight (whew!) dots in them. Examples include Bezariel the Blood-Angel who is a pretty damn powerful Earthbound who has 20 dots of Lores and a Mastery of 4 (meaning he can do shit like immediately raise 100,000 zombies or kill everything within 100,000 yards of himself). However, a powerful enough Methuselah (like Baba-Yaga) can quickly make even an Earthbound as powerful as him into their personal bitch. Which is exactly what Baba Yaga did to him for a couple decades before a Nictuku ashed her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","user":"Oliver the Bold","date":". 05-29-2014, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T21:37:56-07:00","id":152096,"title":"","content":"We are in New York. I think the ST has his own ideas about what is going on in the world, the demon wants me to diablirize anyone of lower gen than me (8th) which I'm actually not that concerned about since I would have ended up doing that anyhow. There is also an Antediluvian sleeping beneath NYC &amp; a cabal of vamps, weres, fera, &amp; a mage plan on finding him &amp; stopping him. I plan on eating him. For some reason the Demon was interested in the Antediluvian as well &amp; was part of the cabal before we killed his Ravnos vessel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T22:28:13-07:00","id":152148,"title":"","content":"The thing is though that most of the advice given here, while sound normally, is invalidated by the fact that you apparently have the ring and carry it around with you. This basically means you cannot do anything, especially the sort of preparations required to take out an Earthbound, without the Demon knowing. Also like said most Earthbound are quite powerful in terms of Lores they have but they also may have access to Mastery which multiplies the lores efficiency allowing them to wipe out cities in one go should they feel like it, ashing a Vampire isn't a big deal for them for the most part, especially ashing a vampire that carries their Reliquary.<br /> <br /> As for the Cult part, considering how well known Moloch is, and that he literally hears when ever someone says his name and can even listen in a bit more if he wishes, it is stretching credibility to claim he has no Cult active. It might be literally anywhere in the world, it matters not since they reap the benefits regardless of destination, so it would be easy for him to keep it concealed from you. Of course if it doesn't have a cult then it means your ST is being extremely benevolent towards you and is likely to provide you with an out of your situation himself without any help from us or rules concerning Earthbound in general. By the way it's ability to listen in on uses of it's own name means that if you go around seeking help against him he will know it regardless of where the Reliquary is, as your character likely has no IC reason to know of this ability of Demons.<br /> <br /> Also the often suggested, get other non-Earthbound demons to help you, plan may backfire horribly as the Earthbound are more than able to enslave other Fallen under their terrible wills. So this might even strengthen the Earthbound expotentially.<br /> <br /> So the best ways to get rid of it are to either destroy it's Reliquary, and why are you alive if you have been able to try this enough to learn that it is almost indestructible, which will send it into Abyss or find a way to cast the Ring away in another Realm. The problem with both is that they are temporary means at best and they tend to piss the Earthbound off so it will be back with a vengeance and both allow it a window of opportunity to fry you then and there. And the hope of getting away from this without consequence is something you should just forget right now, unless the ST want's to give you such an out it is rather impossible, and focus on what is the least painful consequence. Also you should really compare that consequence with being enslaved by it for eternity, is it really that bad or can you become a favored servant?<br /> <br /> Oh, yeah about Possession... Should an Earthbound possess you, by some means, or anyone else really even for a few seconds will mean death for the one being possessed as the Earthbounds power will burn the host down despite what you are.<br /> <br /> So really the only feasible way out is what ever your ST decides to give you but most ST's I know, me included, would likely consider you already screwed and it's about what you do with your Damned situation. So choose whether you want to futily try to fight it, like said it would be a hard thing to do even for an Elder and damn near impossible for a neonate and that is without being actually in touch with the Reliquary, and be in all likelihood destroyed or go with the flow and serve it faithfully, perhaps in the secret hope that someone else comes along at some point in time and succeeds in destroying or Banishing your master. Pretty much any other option you could have is either purposefully presented to you by the ST or really thinking outside the box and succeeding to surprise your ST in such a way that he goes, oh the hell with it and allows you to survive the ordeal.<br /> <br /> So yeah, messing with the Earhtbound is pretty much one of the worst things to do in WoD so good luck with whatever path you may choose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}